.TH XUR.STD.RECORD 7 "2026-11-19" "xur 0.1.3" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.record \- record methods
.SH DESCRIPTION
Records are named-field values (like structs or objects).
.B std::record
is not imported directly; instead these are methods on any record value.
.SH METHODS
.TP
.B get_field(name: str) -> Option<Value>
Return the value of field
.IR name ,
or
.B None
if the record has no such field.
.TP
.B set_field(name: str, value) -> Record
Return a new record with field
.I name
set to
.IR value .
If the field already exists it is replaced; otherwise it is added.
.TP
.B get_method(name: str) -> Option<fn>
Return the callable stored under
.IR name ,
or
.B None
if not present or not callable.
.TP
.B set_method(name: str, func: fn) -> Record
Return a new record with method
.I name
set to
.IR func .
Errors if
.I func
is not callable.
.TP
.B fields() -> [str]
List all field names.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::io;

fn main() {
    let point = #{x: 1, y: 2};
    io::println("fields: {}", point.fields());
    io::println("x = {}", point.get_field("x").unwrap());

    let moved = point.set_field("x", 10);
    io::println("moved.x = {}", moved.get_field("x").unwrap());
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7),
.BR xur.std.map (7)
